---
/**
 * Author page (WEB-FEAT-035; SEO_PLAYBOOK.md §14, CONTENT_GUIDE.md §5 block 3).
 * The owner's own story in first person (sent 2026-10-04, lightly edited: the client numbers and a
 * personal line were removed on his request). Only facts the owner gave: never add credentials,
 * awards or numbers he doesn't have. English only (no reviewed Hindi twin).
 * Photo: owner-supplied, used with permission (design-v4/photo-credits.json "founder-portrait"),
 * cropped from his photo with no retouching: public/media/people/.
 */
import DocPage from '../../../components/trust/DocPage.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { isLive } from '../../../config/pages';
import { site } from '../../../config/site';
import { personSchema } from '../../../lib/schema';

const path = '/about/deepak-chauhan/';
const brand = site.brand;
const name = site.author.name;
const email = site.company.email;
const linkedin = site.author.linkedin;

/** Square face crop for the hero orb (shown at 7rem; 352 px = sharp on 3x screens). */
const PORTRAIT = { src: '/media/people/deepak-chauhan-face-352.webp', alt: `${name}, founder of ${brand}` };
/** 4:5 upper-body crop of the same photo (the source photo is 648 px wide, so 648 is the largest size). */
const PHOTO = {
  avif: '/media/people/deepak-chauhan-portrait-400.avif 400w, /media/people/deepak-chauhan-portrait-648.avif 648w',
  webp: '/media/people/deepak-chauhan-portrait-400.webp 400w, /media/people/deepak-chauhan-portrait-648.webp 648w',
  src: '/media/people/deepak-chauhan-portrait-648.webp',
  width: 648,
  height: 810,
  sizes: '(min-width: 48rem) 16rem, min(20rem, 100vw - 4rem)',
};

const guides = [
  { path: '/palm-reading/', name: 'How to read palm lines' },
  { path: '/hand-lines/', name: 'Lines on your palm and what they mean' },
  { path: '/heart-line/', name: 'Heart line' },
  { path: '/head-line/', name: 'Head line' },
  { path: '/life-line/', name: 'Life line' },
  { path: '/fate-line/', name: 'Fate line' },
  { path: '/is-palmistry-real/', name: 'Is palmistry true?' },
].filter((guide) => isLive(guide.path));

const toc = [
  { id: 'story', label: 'How it started' },
  { id: 'why', label: `Why I built ${brand}` },
  { id: 'guides', label: 'How I write the guides' },
  { id: 'connect', label: 'Let’s connect' },
];

const person = personSchema({ url: PHOTO.src, width: PHOTO.width, height: PHOTO.height });
const profilePage = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  '@id': `${site.baseUrl}${path}#webpage`,
  name: `${name}, founder of ${brand}`,
  url: `${site.baseUrl}${path}`,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  dateModified: '2026-10-04',
  isPartOf: { '@id': `${site.baseUrl}/#website` },
  mainEntity: { '@id': person['@id'] },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${name}, founder of ${brand}`}
  description={`${name} from Nokha, Rajasthan, founded ${brand}. How a failed gaming website led him to semantic SEO, and why he built an honest palm reading app.`}
  path={path}
  locale="en"
  jsonLd={[profilePage, person]}
>
  <DocPage
    crumb={name}
    path={path}
    parents={[{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
    icon="book"
    portrait={PORTRAIT}
    kicker={`Founder of ${brand}`}
    title={name}
    lead={`I build ${brand}, the app and this website, and I write its palmistry guides from the classical books named on each page.`}
    meta="Nokha, Bikaner, Rajasthan, India"
    toc={toc}
  >
    <div class="founder-intro">
      <figure class="founder-photo">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/avif" srcset={PHOTO.avif} sizes={PHOTO.sizes} />
          <img
            src={PHOTO.src}
            srcset={PHOTO.webp}
            sizes={PHOTO.sizes}
            width={PHOTO.width}
            height={PHOTO.height}
            alt={`${name}, founder of ${brand}, in an olive green shirt`}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </picture>
        <figcaption>{name}, founder of {brand}</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="founder-opening">
        <h2 id="story">How it started</h2>
        <p>Hi, I’m {name}, from Nokha in Bikaner, Rajasthan. Let me tell you how it all started.</p>
        <p>
          It began in 2019 and carried on through the lockdown. I was at home and curious about SEO. There was no guidebook and no
          mentor, just me and the internet. I started learning with my cousins, fumbling through keyword research and wondering what
          I was even doing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      Then I launched my first website, a gaming site called techiglu.com. You know what happened? I failed, badly. But that failure
      wasn’t the end. It was the lesson I needed. I didn’t quit; I got smarter.
    </p>
    <p>
      I went deep into SEO and became obsessed with technical audits, semantic SEO and entity-based strategies. By 2023 I had found my
      true love in this work, semantic SEO, and it changed the game for me.
    </p>
    <p>
      I still remember the grind: the late nights reading SEO blogs and trying to work out why my first website tanked. Every day I get
      a little better. I owe a lot of my growth to my SEO guru, Koray Tuğberk GÜBÜR. His teaching has shaped my whole approach.
    </p>
    <p>
      And when I’m not working on websites? I’m gaming hard in Red Dead Redemption, Call of Duty and Battlefield.
    </p>

    <h2 id="why">Why I built {brand}</h2>
    <p>
      Semantic SEO is about meaning: how words, ideas and things connect. Palmistry is an old tradition that a lot of people are
      curious about, and much of what you find about it online is vague or promises things no one can know. I wanted to bring the way I
      work to it: start from your own palm photo, explain each line the way the classical books do, name the book, and say plainly
      what a palm can’t tell you.
    </p>
    <p>
      {brand} is for reflection and entertainment. Palmistry is a tradition, not a science, and I don’t claim otherwise. What I can
      promise is honesty about where every meaning comes from and what a photo can and can’t show.
    </p>

    <h2 id="guides">How I write the guides</h2>
    <p>
      I have built six or more websites and apps, and I build this website and its Android app myself. I write the {brand} guides from
      the classical palmistry books named in each guide’s sources, in plain words and with their limits stated. I’m not a professional
      palm reader: the meanings on this site come from those books, not from personal readings. How every guide is sourced and checked
      is in our <a class="text-link" href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.
    </p>
    {
      guides.length > 0 && (
        <>
          <p>Guides I have written:</p>
          <ul>
            {guides.map((guide) => (
              <li>
                <a class="text-link" href={guide.path}>
                  {guide.name}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </>
      )
    }

    <h2 id="connect">Let’s connect</h2>
    <p>If you want to talk SEO, growth, or maybe even strategy over a game, let’s connect.</p>
    <ul class="founder-links">
      <li>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary founder-link" href={linkedin} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">
          LinkedIn<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {
        email && (
          <li>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary founder-link" href={`mailto:${email}`}>
              {email}
            </a>
          </li>
        )
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">Questions about {brand} itself, your data or a purchase? See the <a class="text-link" href="/about/#contact">contact details</a>.</p>
  </DocPage>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* The photo: a framed glass print beside the opening on wide screens, centred above it on phones. Same content everywhere. */
  .founder-intro { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .founder-photo {
    justify-self: center; width: min(20rem, 100%); margin: 0; padding: 0.5rem; border-radius: var(--r-panel); border: 1px solid transparent;
    background: var(--glass-1) padding-box, var(--rim) border-box; box-shadow: var(--e1), var(--shine);
  }
  .founder-photo img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; object-fit: cover; border-radius: calc(var(--r-panel) - 0.25rem); }
  .founder-photo figcaption { padding: 0.625rem 0.25rem 0.125rem; font-size: var(--fs-caption); color: var(--fg-muted); text-align: center; }
  .founder-opening h2 { margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; }
  :global(.doc-body) ul.founder-links { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .founder-link { min-height: 3rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .founder-intro { grid-template-columns: 16rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; align-items: start; }
    .founder-photo { justify-self: start; width: 100%; }
  }
</style>
